    "text": "If the integral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>,</mo></math> (where&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is the constant of integration and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>), then the minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;",
